---
import { sampleBoxDensity, trapezoidIntegral } from '../../../data/part02/ch07TeachingModels.mjs';

const initial = sampleBoxDensity({ electronCount: 4, orbitalCount: 4, sampleCount: 241 });
const initialIntegral = trapezoidIntegral(initial.samples);
const xScale = (x) => 55 + 650 * x;
const yScale = (density) => 250 - 44 * density;
const pathFor = (samples, key) => samples
  .map((point, index) => `${index === 0 ? 'M' : 'L'} ${xScale(point.x).toFixed(2)} ${yScale(key(point)).toFixed(2)}`)
  .join(' ');
---

<figure class="chapter-visual occupation-density" data-occupation-density>
  <figcaption>
    <strong>原创交互模型：轨道、占据与密度重构</strong>
    <span lang="en">Original interactive model: orbitals, occupations, and density reconstruction</span>
  </figcaption>

  <div class="chapter-visual__controls">
    <label>
      <span>电子数 N | Electron count</span>
      <input type="range" min="1" max="8" step="1" value="4" data-od-electrons />
      <output data-od-electrons-output>4</output>
    </label>
  </div>

  <svg viewBox="0 0 760 315" role="img" aria-labelledby="od-title od-desc">
    <title id="od-title">Density reconstructed from spin-degenerate particle-in-a-box orbitals</title>
    <desc id="od-desc">For one to eight electrons, the lowest one-dimensional box orbitals are filled with at most two electrons each and their occupied orbital densities are summed.</desc>
    <line x1="55" y1="250" x2="705" y2="250" class="plot-axis" />
    <line x1="55" y1="35" x2="55" y2="250" class="plot-axis" />
    <path d={pathFor(initial.samples, (point) => point.density)} class="od-total" data-od-total />
    {initial.occupations.map((occupation, index) => (
      <path
        d={pathFor(initial.samples, (point) => point.orbitalDensities[index])}
        class={`od-orbital od-orbital--${index + 1}`}
        data-od-orbital={index + 1}
        opacity={occupation > 0 ? '1' : '0'}
      />
    ))}
    <text x="705" y="280" text-anchor="end">x/L</text>
    <text x="18" y="55">n(x)</text>
    <text x="55" y="274" text-anchor="middle">0</text>
    <text x="380" y="274" text-anchor="middle">0.5</text>
    <text x="705" y="274" text-anchor="middle">1</text>
  </svg>

  <ul class="od-legend" aria-label="Density curve legend">
    <li><span class="od-key od-key--total"></span>总密度 n(x)</li>
    <li><span class="od-key od-key--1"></span>f₁|φ₁|²</li>
    <li><span class="od-key od-key--2"></span>f₂|φ₂|²</li>
    <li><span class="od-key od-key--3"></span>f₃|φ₃|²</li>
    <li><span class="od-key od-key--4"></span>f₄|φ₄|²</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="chapter-visual__readout" aria-live="polite">
    <span data-od-occupations>occupations = [{initial.occupations.join(', ')}]</span>
    <span data-od-integral>∫₀ᴸ n(x) dx = {initialIntegral.toFixed(6)}</span>
    <strong data-od-kinetic>Ts = {initial.kineticEnergy.toFixed(6)} model energy units</strong>
  </div>

  <div class="chapter-visual__contract">
    <p><strong>模型：</strong>长度 L = 1 的一维无限深势箱，空间轨道 φj(x) = √2 sin(jπx)，每个空间轨道最多容纳两个自旋相反电子。输出为无量纲占据、密度 n(x)（单位 L⁻¹）与辅助动能 Ts（模型单位）。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Model:</strong> a one-dimensional infinite box of length L = 1 with spatial orbitals φj(x) = √2 sin(jπx). Each spatial orbital holds at most two opposite-spin electrons. Outputs are occupations, density in L⁻¹, and auxiliary kinetic energy in model units.</p>
    <p><strong>验收：</strong>占据按 [2,2,…,1,0,…] 填充；任意 N 下数值积分 ∫n dx = N；总密度逐点等于所有已占据轨道密度之和；Ts 等于 Σj fj j²π²/2。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Acceptance:</strong> occupations fill as [2,2,…,1,0,…]; numerical integration gives ∫n dx = N; the total density equals the pointwise sum of occupied-orbital densities; Ts equals Σj fj j²π²/2.</p>
    <p><strong>边界：</strong>该体系没有 Hartree、交换—关联或自洽势，不是材料能带计算。它只验证 Kohn–Sham 辅助体系中轨道、占据、密度和 Ts 的关系。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Boundary:</strong> the model has no Hartree, exchange–correlation, or self-consistent potential and is not a material band calculation. It validates only the relation among auxiliary orbitals, occupations, density, and Ts.</p>
  </div>
</figure>

<script>
  import { sampleBoxDensity, trapezoidIntegral } from '../../../data/part02/ch07TeachingModels.mjs';

  document.querySelectorAll('[data-occupation-density]').forEach((root) => {
    const input = root.querySelector('[data-od-electrons]');
    const output = root.querySelector('[data-od-electrons-output]');
    const totalPath = root.querySelector('[data-od-total]');
    const orbitalPaths = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll('[data-od-orbital]'));
    const occupationsOutput = root.querySelector('[data-od-occupations]');
    const integralOutput = root.querySelector('[data-od-integral]');
    const kineticOutput = root.querySelector('[data-od-kinetic]');
    if (!(input instanceof HTMLInputElement) || !(totalPath instanceof SVGPathElement)) return;

    const xScale = (x) => 55 + 650 * x;
    const yScale = (density) => 250 - 44 * density;
    const pathFor = (samples, key) => samples
      .map((point, index) => `${index === 0 ? 'M' : 'L'} ${xScale(point.x).toFixed(2)} ${yScale(key(point)).toFixed(2)}`)
      .join(' ');

    const update = () => {
      const electronCount = Number.parseInt(input.value, 10);
      const result = sampleBoxDensity({ electronCount, orbitalCount: 4, sampleCount: 241 });
      const integral = trapezoidIntegral(result.samples);
      totalPath.setAttribute('d', pathFor(result.samples, (point) => point.density));
      orbitalPaths.forEach((path, index) => {
        if (!(path instanceof SVGPathElement)) return;
        path.setAttribute('d', pathFor(result.samples, (point) => point.orbitalDensities[index]));
        path.setAttribute('opacity', result.occupations[index] > 0 ? '1' : '0');
      });
      if (output instanceof HTMLOutputElement) output.value = String(electronCount);
      if (occupationsOutput instanceof HTMLElement) occupationsOutput.textContent = `occupations = [${result.occupations.join(', ')}]`;
      if (integralOutput instanceof HTMLElement) integralOutput.textContent = `∫₀ᴸ n(x) dx = ${integral.toFixed(6)}`;
      if (kineticOutput instanceof HTMLElement) kineticOutput.textContent = `Ts = ${result.kineticEnergy.toFixed(6)} model energy units`;
    };

    input.addEventListener('input', update);
    update();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .occupation-density svg { width: 100%; max-height: 24rem; }
  .occupation-density text { fill: currentColor; font-size: 14px; }
  .od-total, .od-orbital { fill: none; }
  .od-total { stroke: var(--sl-color-text-accent); stroke-width: 4; }
  .od-orbital { stroke-width: 2; stroke-dasharray: 7 5; }
  .od-orbital--1 { stroke: var(--sl-color-accent-high); }
  .od-orbital--2 { stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3); }
  .od-orbital--3 { stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-4); }
  .od-orbital--4 { stroke: currentColor; }
  .od-legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem 1rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .od-key { display: inline-block; width: 1.7rem; margin-right: 0.35rem; border-top: 3px solid currentColor; vertical-align: middle; }
  .od-key--total { color: var(--sl-color-text-accent); }
  .od-key--1 { color: var(--sl-color-accent-high); border-top-style: dashed; }
  .od-key--2 { color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); border-top-style: dashed; }
  .od-key--3 { color: var(--sl-color-gray-4); border-top-style: dashed; }
  .od-key--4 { border-top-style: dashed; }
</style>
